			"notes": "- Lead arrows: a lead and an arrow crafted together. Where one sticks its lead runs back to you, held at the length it flew, to climb by sneaking. Click a fence to tie it off there; shoot a creature to put it on a lead.\n- A rope tied off at both ends, an arrow's lead at a fence or a lead from post to post, is climbed as a lead in hand is: sneak to take hold and climb, jump to drop a step, K to let go.\n- Villagers, wandering traders, zombie villagers and piglins can be put on a lead.\n- Hanging from a lead is steady: the lead's pull now reaches the player hanging on it, who no longer bobs.\n- Rappelling: each jump drops you a step down the rope, and holding sneak climbs back up.\n- With Block Tip 1.2, the reading stays up on its card instead of the action bar."
		},
